abstract: >-
  Metric-Differential-Tree UTN and Context-Bound Token Intelligence
  (MDT-UTN-CBT) presents an algorithmic framework for converting context
  into explicit structural identity, Universal Typing and Naming (UTN),
  Context-Bound Tokens (CBT), and reusable context-addressed intelligence.
  The framework represents target context through GenericContainerStarmap,
  organizes structural similarity and difference through a
  Metric-Differential Tree (MDT), applies Per-Node UTN Intelligence for
  typing-first and naming-second structural decisions, and exposes the
  resulting identity through Context-Bound Tokens using the canonical
  notation token@context. The repository further introduces
  Baseline-Preserved Context Injection for controlled measurement of
  explicit context influence, and develops Context-as-Address as a common
  structural interface for search, caching, Delta Intelligence, CCC,
  Brain-Unit dispatch, validation, and structural growth.

